s_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/deployments","created_at":"2014-03-16T16:19:57Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T14:25:40Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T13:53:05Z","git_url":"git://github.com/rclone/rclone.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:rclone/rclone.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/rclone/rclone.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/rclone/rclone","homepage":"https://rclone.org","size":216098,"stargazers_count":54045,"watchers_count":54045,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":4794,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1082,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["azure-blob","azure-blob-storage","azure-files","backblaze-b2","cloud-storage","dropbox","encryption","ftp","fuse-filesystem","go","golang","google-cloud-storage","google-drive","onedrive","openstack-swift","rclone","s3","sftp","sync","webdav"],"visibility":"public","forks":4794,"open_issues":1082,"watchers":54045,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Hey @ncw, have you thought about building rclone with Bazel before?\r\n\r\nFirst off, the primary *disadvantage* is that Bazel has a very steep learning curve. If you're not already familiar with it, maybe it's not worth the investment and additional complexity.\r\n\r\nIt has a number of really nice properties:\r\n\r\n* Sandboxing.\r\n  * While writing tests in cmd/gitannex/, I've occasionally found my buggy code creating files in surprising places, due to mangled paths/filenames. If we could run tests with Bazel, they'd be automatically sandboxed. Attempts to write files outside the sandbox would crash the test! (You can also relax the sandboxing as needed, but it's a nice default.)\r\n  * Sandboxed builds would also help with bugs like #8092.\r\n  * Another use case: the gitannex e2e tests require an up-to-date `rclone` binary. Currently, we just do our darnedest and [check the version output](https://github.com/rclone/rclone/blob/f8d782c02de5e42c354f281b4f32c4128fa5db1e/cmd/gitannex/e2e_test.go#L21-L24) of whichever `rclone` we find. We could actually write this dependency explicitly with Bazel and drop the heuristic. (That is, the test target, `//cmd/gitannex:gitannex_test`, would explicitly depend on the rclone binary, `//:rclone`.)\r\n\r\n* Faster builds. Bazel is extremely good at caching. If you configure a disk cache, you would wait approximately zero seconds to build a binary that you already built months ago. This is super useful when you're bouncing back and forth between commits while debugging. (It also caches test results!)\r\n  * More generally, Bazel enables [hermetic builds](https://bazel.build/basics/hermeticity). Perhaps we trust the go toolchain enough that binaries don't have to match byte-for-byte, but it's a nice property to have that the same inputs produce the same outputs.\r\n\r\n* You can also use Bazel to pull in arbitrary dependencies.\r\n  * This is a sort of half-baked idea, but I'm imagining some of the Azure pipelines stuff, which can only run in the cloud, could be Bazelified to enable running it locally.\r\n  * We could pull in specific releases of git-annex and [git-annex-remote-rclone](https://github.com/git-annex-remote-rclone/git-annex-remote-rclone) for e2e and compat testing. Maybe not the highest priority, but I hope it illustrates the capability.\r\n\r\nI recently discovered that [Gazelle](https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel-gazelle) is a thing — it can mostly automatically generate the necessary `BUILD` files for a Go project. It's pretty neat and does a lot of tedious work, but it's not 100% automatic (I tried!).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/8093/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/8093/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/comments/2367686696","html_url":"https://github.com/rclone/rclone/issues/8092#issuecomment-2367686696","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/8092","id":2367686696,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAQ-n5M6NIAgo","user":{"login":"albertony","id":12441419,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDQxNDE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12441419?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony","html_url":"https://github.com/albertony","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-23T09:33:59Z","updated_at":"2024-09-23T09:33:59Z","body":"I think the point is that we want the literal `$HOME` and `$USER` to be present in the generated docs for publishing on rclone.org, not the expanded values from the build system. Maybe this command should run with `--config /notfound` or something to stop it from creating config on disk (https://rclone.org/docs/#config-config-file).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/comments/2367686696/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"albertony","id":12441419,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDQxNDE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12441419?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony","html_url":"https://github.com/albertony","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albertony/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/comments/2368543485","html_url":"https://github.com/rclone/rclone/issues/8092#issuecomment-2368543485","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/8092","id":2368543485,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAQ-n5M6NLRr9","user":{"login":"dmcardle","id":183652,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzY1Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183652?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmcardle","html_url":"https://github.com/dmcardle","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmcardle/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmcardle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmcardle/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmcardle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmcardle/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmcardle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmcardle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmcardle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmcardle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-23T14:57:52Z","updated_at":"2024-09-23T14:57:52Z","body":"Ah, thanks! I think you're right about this being a hack to so that `$HOME` appears in the docs. Neat trick, I didn't realize `/notfound` was special. It would mean the docs would say `/notfound` instead of `$HOME` though, right?\r\n\r\nAnother possible solution is to use a placeholder name and then search/replace with sed. I find it a little confusing/terrifying to instruct a Makefile to delete `'$HOME'`, whether single quoted or not, and this way we don't have to.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n commanddocs: rclone\r\n-       XDG_CACHE_HOME=\"\" XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"\" HOME=\"\\$$HOME\" USER=\"\\$$USER\" rclone gendocs docs/content/\r\n+       XDG_CACHE_HOME=\"\" XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"\" HOME=\"tmpFakeHomeDirForDocGen\" USER=\"\\$$USER\" rclone gendocs docs/content/\r\n+       find docs -name '*.md' -exec sed -i tmpFakeHomeDirForDocGen '$HOME' {} \\;\r\n+       rmdir -p tmpFakeHomeDirForDocGen/.config/rclone/\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlternatively, maybe config.go should be a little more careful about when it creates these directories. Right now, it happens in `makeConfigPath()` which is called by `init()`!  https://github.com/rclone/rclone/blob/f8d782c02de5e42c354f281b4f32c4128fa5db1e/fs/config/config.go#L283","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/comments/2368543485/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"dmcardle","id":183652,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzY1Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183652?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.co